							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg12838#msg12838">Quote from: Ssnakess on November 26, 2004, 06:51:04 pm</a></div><div class="quote">Why everyone insists on calling Ascent new and old is beyond me</div>I call them the new and the original, if that sounds better to you!<br /><br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote"> we didn&#039;t reform, we lost as many people as FoT has lost recently. Why not divide FoT into two timeframes?</div>Because there was never anything worth remembering in FoT. No more than in EiE, DA or whatever. However for example AoD/AL was certainly split by timeframes from when it was run by Dyvim and the Crimshines in a serverwide competition of ownage to the squad of Axine puppets trying to &quot;destroy&quot; Ascent during Velious and Luclin.<br /><br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">I realize that someone will insist its because Ascent changed leadership,  but in that case, then the current EiE is the &quot;new&quot; EiE too?</div>If their ability to raid drops significantly all of a sudden and if EiE is somehow badass enough already (wouldn&#039;t really know), then why not?<br /><br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote"> But you can compare current guilds, and we are still well ahead of them.</div>This, however, seems completely valid from all I&#039;ve seen and heard.
